===============================================================================
PURPOSE
===============================================================================

Advancement & Paid Refereeing is the primary development-pathway page for
Cypress AYSO Region 154 referees.

This page is designed to:

- Encourage referees to continue developing after Regional certification.
- Explain the AYSO referee badge progression at a high level.
- Help referees create a development plan with the RRA and referee mentors.
- Explain the role of experience, training, mentoring and assessment.
- Introduce referee-instructor, assessor and leadership opportunities.
- Clearly distinguish AYSO volunteer certification from U.S. Soccer licensing.
- Explain the separate Cal South and NOCRA paid-referee pathway.
- Explain that paid assignments are not automatic or guaranteed.
- Explain AYSO and U.S. Soccer cross-certification at a high level.
- Route referees to official current requirements rather than publishing
  fees, course dates or standards that may change.
- Connect users to every redesigned referee page.
- Provide local and cross-page navigation without JavaScript.

===============================================================================
IMPORTANT PATHWAY DISTINCTION
===============================================================================

AYSO VOLUNTEER REFEREE PATH:

- Regional Referee
- Intermediate Referee
- Advanced Referee
- National Referee
- Mentoring
- Instruction
- Assessment
- Regional, Area and Section leadership

U.S. SOCCER / CAL SOUTH / NOCRA PATH:

- Separate U.S. Soccer referee license
- Current Cal South registration and risk-management requirements
- Current SafeSport requirements when applicable
- Current status on the Cal South Registered Officials List
- Membership or onboarding with a referee association such as NOCRA
- Assignments offered through approved assignors or associations

An AYSO badge does not automatically create a U.S. Soccer license.

A U.S. Soccer license does not automatically complete Region 154 volunteer
eligibility or AYSO requirements.

Cross-certification may be available when the referee meets the current
requirements of both programs.

