        <section class="r154-advance-section" id="cross-certification" aria-labelledby="cross-certification-title">

            <div class="r154-advance-section-heading">

                <span class="r154-advance-eyebrow">
                    Referees With Experience in Another Program
                </span>

                <h2 class="r154-advance-section-title" id="cross-certification-title">
                    AYSO and U.S. Soccer Cross-Certification
                </h2>

                <p class="r154-advance-section-intro">
                    AYSO provides a cross-certification process for eligible
                    referees who hold certification in one system but not the
                    other.
                </p>

            </div>


            <div class="r154-advance-cross-grid">

                <article class="r154-advance-cross-card">

                    <span class="r154-advance-cross-label">
                        U.S. Soccer to AYSO
                    </span>

                    <h3>
                        Experienced U.S. Soccer Referees Joining AYSO
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        The referee may request review for the applicable AYSO
                        certification while still completing Region 154
                        volunteer registration, safety and eligibility
                        requirements.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-advance-cross-card">

                    <span class="r154-advance-cross-label">
                        AYSO to U.S. Soccer
                    </span>

                    <h3>
                        Experienced AYSO Referees Entering Cal South
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        An eligible AYSO referee may use the current crossover
                        process, but must still complete all applicable U.S.
                        Soccer and Cal South licensing requirements.
                    </p>

                </article>

            </div>


            <div class="r154-advance-cross-note">

                <strong>
                    Cross-certification is not automatic.
                </strong>

                Requirements may include minimum time holding the original
                certification, documentation, review, fees, current training
                and approval from the appropriate program administrators.

            </div>


