        <section class="r154-advance-section">

            <div class="r154-advance-section-heading">

                <span class="r154-advance-eyebrow">
                    Common Development and Paid-Referee Questions
                </span>

                <h2 class="r154-advance-section-title">
                    Advancement &amp; Paid Refereeing FAQ
                </h2>

            </div>


            <div class="r154-advance-faq-grid">

                <article class="r154-advance-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        What comes after Regional Referee?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        The next AYSO badge is generally Intermediate Referee,
                        subject to the current training, experience, service
                        and assessment requirements.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-advance-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        Is completing an Intermediate course enough?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        No. Badge advancement may also require documented
                        experience, service, observation, assessment and an
                        approved application.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-advance-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        How do I know whether I am ready to advance?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Discuss your current experience and development goals
                        with the RRA and request mentoring on appropriate
                        assignments.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-advance-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        May a youth referee earn higher AYSO badges?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Youth referees may continue developing, subject to the
                        current age, experience and certification requirements.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-advance-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        Must I pursue a higher badge?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        No. Referees may continue serving successfully at their
                        current certification while developing experience and
                        confidence.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-advance-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        How do I request a mentor?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Email the RRA with your badge, assignment experience,
                        development goal and upcoming availability.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-advance-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        Does an AYSO badge allow me to referee paid games?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Not automatically. Paid U.S. Soccer-affiliated matches
                        require the current U.S. Soccer and Cal South licensing
                        process.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-advance-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        Does U.S. Soccer certification replace AYSO compliance?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        No. Region 154 volunteers must still complete the
                        applicable AYSO registration, safety and eligibility
                        requirements.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-advance-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        What is NOCRA?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        NOCRA is a local referee association serving Cypress
                        and surrounding communities and assigning referees to
                        eligible competitions.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-advance-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        Does joining NOCRA guarantee assignments?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        No. Assignments depend on current standing,
                        availability, experience, performance, competition
                        demand and assignor decisions.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-advance-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        Can my AYSO experience help with U.S. Soccer licensing?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        A crossover process may be available. Review the
                        current Cal South and AYSO cross-certification
                        requirements.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-advance-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        Where should I begin?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Begin by identifying your goal, checking your current
                        certification record and contacting the appropriate
                        referee administrator.
                    </p>

                </article>

